  "classIri": "urn:ngm:class:deep-generative-model",
  "domain": "machine-learning",
  "definition": "A Deep Generative Model is a class of deep neural network trained to learn and approximate the underlying probability distribution of a dataset so that novel, statistically plausible samples can be drawn from it. The principal families \u2014 Generative Adversarial Networks (GANs), Variational Autoencoders (VAEs), normalising flows, and diffusion models \u2014 differ in how they parameterise and optimise the generative distribution, offering distinct trade-offs among sample fidelity, mode coverage, training stability, and latent-space interpretability. These models underpin modern generative AI capabilities across images, audio, video, text, and structured scientific data such as molecular graphs.",
